BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Contempt (1963)
DTSTART:20261008T023000Z
DTEND:20261008T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20261008T023000Z
UID:R5NOmEaDHN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesA film producer 
 (Jack Palance) and his director (pantheon director Fritz Lang) are filming
  Homer’s The Odyssey. The screenwriter (Michel Piccoli) and his stunning
  wife (Brigitte Bardot) are on the scene. Godard seeks to “film thought\
 , the beauty of moments\,” and a small emotional miscalculation (or happ
 enstance) sows doubt in a Mediterranean paradise.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/
 programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/contempt\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salome's Last Dance (1988)
DTSTART:20261010T210000Z
DTEND:20261010T224500Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T210000Z
UID:ReGLUcv705
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nPresented by SIFF and the Seattl
 e Opera\, in conjunction with their production of "Salome."On Guy Fawkes N
 ight\, Oscar Wilde goes to a luxury brothel where the owner has prepared a
  surprise for the renowned author: a private and very special performance 
 of his banned play "Salome."\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/sa
 lomes-last-dance\n\nEstimated start: 14:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Le Bonheur (Happiness) (1965)
DTSTART:20261015T023000Z
DTEND:20261015T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20261015T023000Z
UID:Enp64v38T5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesIn a French Impre
 ssionist landscape of sunny blossoms\, a blissful husband and wife (Jean-C
 laude and Claire Drouot) picnic on the grass. Their happiness feels organi
 cally grown\, part of the natural order. But when Jean-Claude meets a post
 al clerk (Marie-France Boyer)\, he realizes he has a capacity for “more 
 flowers\, more apples.”\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouv
 elles-femmes/le-bonheur-(happiness)\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carrie (1976)
DTSTART:20261011T223000Z
DTEND:20261012T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20261011T223000Z
UID:XLAEPL8Pc2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nWelcome to the first installment 
 of SIFF Book Club! We are reading Stephen King's "Carrie" and then watchin
 g it on the big screen for the 50th anniversary.Brian De Palma’s 1976 l
 andmark supernatural horror film\, based on Stephen King’s first novel\,
  resulted in an Oscar® nomination for Sissy Spacek’s portrayal of a tee
 naged social outcast wielding fatal telekinetic powers.  Arrive early to 
 peruse a selection of books from Mercer Street Books. Local artists Chloe 
 Ladwig and Max B will be selling prints\, stickers\, and more featuring th
 e Carrie White. Festival Senior Programmer Dan Doody will be introducing t
 he screening\, providing some book-to-film context before we meet afterwar
 ds for our Book Club discussion at The Traveling Goat.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/programs-and-events/siff-book-club/carrie\n\nEstimated start: 15:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Hitcher (1986)
DTSTART:20261016T020000Z
DTEND:20261016T035500Z
DTSTAMP:20261016T020000Z
UID:PxCaq8rbON
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nOn a dark and stormy night\, fati
 gued driver Jim Halsey (C. Thomas Howell) picks up a mysterious hitchhiker
  (Rutger Hauer)\, leading to a terrifying cat-and-mouse nightmare along th
 e highways of the American southwest.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and
 -events/the-open-road/the-hitcher\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Matchstick Productions Presents\, "The Way Out" 2026 Ski Film
DTSTART:20261021T023000Z
DTEND:20261021T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20261021T023000Z
UID:VT4Y8B8EuK
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 60 mins (1h00m)\n\nMatchstick Productions returns wi
 th their 34th annual ski film\, The Way Out\, a raw tribute to the timeles
 s culture and lifestyle of skiing. Dropping you straight into heavy Alaska
 n spine lines\, deep Japanese powder\, and iconic Swiss villages. This fil
 m shows skiing as far more than a sport\; it’s a path toward total freed
 om. From legendary veterans to rising breakout talent\, the message is sim
 ple: the soul of skiing isn’t dead\; it's waiting wherever snow falls. 
 VIP tickets include premium seating and gift bag from Matchstick Productio
